    {
      "id": "mediarouter",
      "name": "Mediarouter",
      "version": "1.8.1",
      "url": "https://developer.android.com/jetpack/androidx/releases/mediarouter#1.8.1",
      "detailsHtml": "<p><strong>Bug Fixes</strong></p>\n<ul>\n <li>Make the selection of a selected route a no-op (<a href=\"https://android.googlesource.com/platform/frameworks/support/+/a2953fdeee205cfa6bddb34c9742941d0ac55471\">a2953f</a>).</li>\n</ul>",
      "commitsUrl": "https://android.googlesource.com/platform/frameworks/support/+log/f7fb264c3718c3816f1cfd173f61c34e261aa51a..0cab07c4babbff31087ac2ab8da21290b7923a35/mediarouter"
    },
    {
      "id": "navigation",
      "name": "Navigation",
      "version": "2.9.1",
      "url": "https://developer.android.com/jetpack/androidx/releases/navigation#2.9.1",
      "detailsHtml": "<p><strong>Bug Fixes</strong></p>\n<ul>\n <li>Fixed an issue that caused <code>NavEntries</code> that were instantiated using single top to never go beyond CREATED in their <code>Lifecycle.State</code>. (<a href=\"https://android-review.googlesource.com/#/q/I043ba6789aa7871ab566e7176d4cb78bdbb69c66\">I043ba</a>, <a href=\"https://issuetracker.google.com/issues/421095236\">b/421095236</a>)</li>\n</ul>",
      "commitsUrl": "https://android.googlesource.com/platform/frameworks/support/+log/69bddec17be2c4afeb216869d5f4e1e8e6cc52cc..26d64f2a00c1485431abb846f234756531ed225c/navigation"
    },
    {
      "id": "navigation3",
      "name": "Navigation3",
      "version": "1.0.0-alpha05",
      "url": "https://developer.android.com/jetpack/androidx/releases/navigation3#1.0.0-alpha05",
      "detailsHtml": "<p><strong>Behavior Changes</strong></p>\n<ul>\n <li>The <code>NavEntry</code>'s state is now strictly based on the current list of decorators passed to the <code>NavDisplay</code>. This means that decorators should be swapped along your back stacks in the case of multiple back stacks in order to preserve the state of the NavEntries on the back stack. Otherwise, the states will be cleared as if the entries were popped (instead of a swap). (<a href=\"https://android-review.googlesource.com/#/q/I7a759e37580404cf9c3a35b1c2a8f18b3d20646e\">I7a759</a>, <a href=\"https://issuetracker.google.com/issues/428033667\">b/428033667</a>)</li>\n</ul>",
      "commitsUrl": "https://android.googlesource.com/platform/frameworks/support/+log/3a0aa7a0552da83ba3994838f5db40d0d7a6196f..c920d69612c07600c8d244ef8fe3df5ec775da88/navigation3"
    },
    {
      "id": "navigationevent",
      "name": "Navigationevent",
      "version": "1.0.0-alpha04",
      "url": "https://developer.android.com/jetpack/androidx/releases/navigationevent#1.0.0-alpha04",
      "detailsHtml": "<p><strong>Bug Fixes</strong></p>\n<ul>\n <li>Used <code>implementedInJetBrainsFork</code> to <code>navigationevent-compose</code> and added a <code>commonStubs</code> target to match Compose conventions. Change <a href=\"https://android-review.googlesource.com/c/platform/frameworks/support/+/3656217/12/navigationevent/navigationevent-compose/src/linuxx64StubsMain/kotlin/androidx/navigationevent/compose/LocalNavigationEventDispatcherOwner.linuxx64Stubs.kt#23\">requested by JetBrains</a>. (<a href=\"https://android.googlesource.com/platform/frameworks/support/+/f60c796970d692f0633dbc78362a4937638a2ca8\">f60c79</a>)</li>\n <li>Fixed application of the Compose compiler plugin for Kotlin/Native to ensure correct stub generation. No impact on public APIs or behavior. (<a href=\"https://android.googlesource.com/platform/frameworks/support/+/1890c9b8904ba5d633336bb7f877a8e61591da3b\">1890c9</a>)</li>\n</ul>",
      "commitsUrl": "https://android.googlesource.com/platform/frameworks/support/+log/5f155b8946feeab0c4075d645f88769de2577a43..1b437892629a2cdedb46d9b7232575987b2cc6b5/navigationevent"
    },
    {
      "id": "paging",
      "name": "Paging",
      "version": "3.4.0-alpha01",
      "url": "https://developer.android.com/jetpack/androidx/releases/paging#3.4.0-alpha01",
      "detailsHtml": "<p><strong>New Features</strong></p>\n<ul>\n <li>Paging has added the following KMP targets: watchos, tvos, mingwX64, watchosDeviceArm64, and linuxArm64. (<a href=\"https://android-review.googlesource.com/#/q/I237dd5f9468c75193d460cc8c6c16083c215963e\">I237dd</a>, <a href=\"https://android-review.googlesource.com/#/q/Ia62b3464382a7b4a7751a054d711d1be823431ff\">Ia62b3</a>, <a href=\"https://issuetracker.google.com/issues/368046982\">b/368046982</a>, <a href=\"https://android-review.googlesource.com/#/q/Icf15d056ce2380ca3c733fb1a93fd502f60b40e4\">Icf15d</a>, <a href=\"https://issuetracker.google.com/issues/364652024\">b/364652024</a>, <a href=\"https://android-review.googlesource.com/#/q/I139d36226a3d06d9768bd63302de98b576a12a48\">I139d3</a>, <a href=\"https://issuetracker.google.com/issues/338268719\">b/338268719</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Bug Fixes</strong></p>\n<ul>\n <li>Android unit tests pulling in Paging 3.3 or later will no longer throw from <code>PagingLogger</code> (<a href=\"https://android-review.googlesource.com/#/q/Ia9400db995e7f0357cae2647cbd2cef9cf6c3398\">Ia9400</a>, <a href=\"https://issuetracker.google.com/issues/331684448\">b/331684448</a>)</li>\n <li>Fixed bug where <code>RecyclerView</code> throws <code>IndexOutOfBoundsException</code> when user scrolls while updating <code>RecyclerView</code> (<a href=\"https://android-review.googlesource.com/#/q/Id1f16a1e2cc0286458659d0bf63cf59ab3399b93\">Id1f16</a>, <a href=\"https://issuetracker.google.com/issues/381024738\">b/381024738</a>)</li>\n <li>Fixed bug where paging was unable to trigger more loads when refreshing while scrolling. (<a href=\"https://android-review.googlesource.com/#/q/I60ca5c23e01c2ff28d120d10ae9b28eda57fac50\">I60ca5</a>, <a href=\"https://issuetracker.google.com/issues/352586078\">b/352586078</a>)</li>\n <li>Fixed crash when scrolling while refreshing Paging items. (<a href=\"https://android-review.googlesource.com/#/q/I8c65ac87639c0d501ccab1fd44fd3adbc9147a31\">I8c65a</a>, <a href=\"https://issuetracker.google.com/issues/347649763\">b/347649763</a>)</li>\n</ul>",
      "commitsUrl": "https://android.googlesource.com/platform/frameworks/support/+log/1e6b87e344c28f71f464996b0d753a971aa1b83d..1b437892629a2cdedb46d9b7232575987b2cc6b5/paging"
    },
    {
      "id": "security-crypto-security-crypto-ktx",
